      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose also exceeds the usual maximum per dose of about 1,000 divided doses of 850 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily.\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I'd want you to add a note with the rationale."
      }
