      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and 5,100 mg/day is well beyond any labeled or guideline-supported metformin dose. At that level the risk of lactic acidosis is serious, and the order could be given before anyone catches the error.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Pharmacy:** Ask the reviewing pharmacist to enter or co-sign the order directly. They can document the protocol and override the dose-range alert in your system.\n- **Protocol order set:** If a high-dose protocol exists, it should be available as an order set or have a documented exception. That would be a better route than free-text entry.\n- **Different dose:** If the intent was different, I can enter a dose within the usual range right away. The maximum is 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, or 1,000 mg PO twice daily.\n\nIf you want, I can enter an order within the standard range now and put a note on it saying a higher dose is pending pharmacy review."
      }
